---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSpread from '../components/HeroSpread.astro';
import MrzStrip from '../components/MrzStrip.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="UniDPP" eyebrow="Overview">
  <h1>An international framework for the Digital Product Passport</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    UniDPP treats every regulatory regime — the European Union's EN&nbsp;18216–18246 series
    among them — as one profile on a neutral international core: one product identity, one
    append-only record, many jurisdiction, sector, and characteristic lenses, with trust that
    crosses borders without requiring anyone to adopt anyone else's rules.
  </p>

  <HeroSpread />
  <MrzStrip />

  <section class="plate" aria-labelledby="path-heading">
    <h2 id="path-heading">Read by depth</h2>
    <p>
      The site is arranged as one sequence, from plain language to the full reference
      material. Each level assumes the one before it.
    </p>
    <ol class="path">
      <li>
        <a href="/learn/">
          <span class="pnum">01</span>
          <span class="plbl">
            <strong>Understand</strong>
            <span>What a Digital Product Passport is, told with a washing machine.</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/why/">
          <span class="pnum">02</span>
          <span class="plbl">
            <strong>Why international</strong>
            <span>One laptop, five jurisdictions, one record instead of five.</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/how/">
          <span class="pnum">03</span>
          <span class="plbl">
            <strong>How it works</strong>
            <span>The six layers, the fourteen invariants, capability classes, trust.</span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/reference/">
          <span class="pnum">04</span>
          <span class="plbl">
            <strong>Reference</strong>
            <span>
              The framework in full, the standards map, the implementation, comparisons,
              trust, papers, terminology, and stewardship.
            </span>
          </span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="work-heading">
    <h2 id="work-heading">The work</h2>
    <p>
      The framework and its reference implementation are developed in the open at
      <a href="https://github.com/unidpp">github.com/unidpp</a>, under Apache-2.0 / MIT
      licences, with published conformance suites. Standards contributions are carried to
      ISO/IEC JTC 5 and partner bodies through liaison channels; the project does not create
      a rival standards track. Stewardship is shared across the bodies that already operate
      each layer — see <a href="/reference/about/">about</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .path {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--hairline);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    max-width: none;
  }
  .path a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3.2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.9rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .path a:hover {
    background: #fff;
  }
  .path li + li a {
    border-top: 0;
  }
  .pnum {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--navy);
  }
  .plbl {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .plbl strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .plbl span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
</style>
